    "description": "• Led the development and deployment of dynamic websites utilizing WordPress, HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and PHP, focusing on advanced UI/UX strategies to enhance client satisfaction and engagement. \n• Directed and mentored a team of 9 interns across two locations (Camden, NJ and Kensington, PA), significantly improving project delivery by implementing structured feedback loops, comprehensive evaluations, and targeted skill enhancement programs. \n• Played a pivotal role in integrating Hopeworks' trauma-informed approach, aligning project objectives with broader business and community development goals, thereby fostering an inclusive and supportive work environment. \n• Drove cross-functional collaboration with design, marketing, and sales teams to innovate and elevate product quality, ensuring alignment with client expectations and market trends. \n• Enhanced organizational culture and intern retention by applying trauma-informed management practices, which increased team cohesion and optimized performance metrics. \n• Architected and executed sophisticated user interface/user experience designs, prioritizing accessibility to meet web standards, which broadened market reach and reinforced client relationships. \n• Championed the quality assurance process, refining system operations to elevate project throughput and accuracy, resulting in heightened client trust and repeat business.",
